So, not to ask a stupid question, but I am curious. Why are we doing all of
this via text?

Bandwidth. The less data needs to be transmitted, the better it can be hidden
and secured. This system uses approximately one bit per letter, or one byte per
word. Voice would be an order of magnitude more.

plus he sent that in like two seconds so either he types faster than liszt or
he had it written up and ready to go

It all comes down to information theory. And in this case a large corpus of my
writing and a chorded keyboard.

